---
import PublicLayout from '../layouts/PublicLayout.astro';

const updated = '20 November 2026';
---

<PublicLayout
  title="Privacy policy — Hustler Community Opportunities"
  description="How Hustler Community Opportunities handles data: anonymous analytics, public submissions, admin authentication, third-party processors, retention and your choices."
>
  <header class="page-head">
    <div class="container">
      <nav class="breadcrumbs" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
        <a href="/">Home</a><span class="sep">/</span><span aria-current="page">Privacy</span>
      </nav>
      <div class="page-head__inner" style="margin-top:1.25rem">
        <div>
          <span class="eyebrow eyebrow--brand">Legal</span>
          <h1>Privacy policy</h1>
          <p>A short, concrete description of what this site stores and why. Last updated {updated}.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </header>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container--narrow prose">
      <h2>Who we are</h2>
      <p>
        Hustler Community Opportunities (“the directory”) is a curated opportunity directory operated as part of the
        Hustler Community. The public site is at this domain; the community is on
        <a href="https://www.linkedin.com/company/hustlercommunity" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"
          >our official LinkedIn page</a
        >.
      </p>

      <h2>What we collect</h2>
      <h3>Browsing the directory</h3>
      <p>
        You can browse and search without an account. We record anonymous aggregate events — a page view, an outbound
        application click, a share or a search query — against a listing or in aggregate. These events do not include
        your name, email address, IP address or user agent, and we do not create a profile of you. Search queries are
        stored as short strings for aggregate reporting and are not linked to an identity.
      </p>
      <p>
        The public pages use <code>sessionStorage</code> in your browser to avoid counting the same view or search twice
        in one session. That value stays in your browser and is not sent to us as an identifier. We do not use
        advertising cookies or third-party analytics scripts.
      </p>

      <h3>Submitting an opportunity or a report</h3>
      <p>
        The public suggestion form asks for a source URL and details about the role. The report form asks for the reason
        for the report, optional details, and an optional contact email. If you provide a contact email, we use it only
        to follow up on that report. Submissions and reports are reviewed by an editor; they are not published
        automatically.
      </p>
      <p>
        Source text you paste or submit is stored privately for review and is never exposed on the public site. Public
        listing pages contain only the reviewed, structured fields.
      </p>

      <h3>Continuing to an employer application</h3>
      <p>
        Before you continue to an employer's application page, you may provide your email and consent to its collection.
        We send a one-time code to verify that address. While the code is pending, the address is held temporarily for
        up to 10 minutes; failed or expired requests are not added to candidate records. Hashed email and network
        identifiers used to enforce sending limits are deleted in the daily cleanup after two days. After successful verification,
        we store the verified email with the job you selected to understand candidate interest and improve the directory.
        We do not send your email to the employer, use it to create an account, or send marketing email. You can request
        deletion through the report form.
      </p>

      <h3>Admin workspace</h3>
      <p>
        The admin workspace is restricted to allowlisted administrators. Sign-in uses Supabase Auth. Session tokens are
        stored in HttpOnly, SameSite=Lax cookies; they are not readable by client-side JavaScript. Admin activity is
        logged for accountability (actor, action, entity and time).
      </p>

      <h2>Third-party processors</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Supabase</strong> — database and authentication hosting.</li>
        <li><strong>Vercel</strong> — application hosting. Cloudflare Turnstile may be used for bot protection on public forms.</li>
        <li><strong>Resend</strong> — delivery of the one-time verification email when candidate email verification is enabled.</li>
        <li><strong>Groq</strong> (default) or <strong>Google Gemini</strong> when configured - pasted or retrieved source text is sent server-side to extract structured fields. The integration is used for extraction only; the model does not publish anything.</li>
        <li><strong>Telegram</strong> — when the owner bot is configured, the owner can submit a source and receive a review preview. Telegram processes those messages under its own terms.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        These providers process data on our behalf to run the service. We do not sell personal data or share it for
        advertising.
      </p>

      <h2>Retention</h2>
      <p>
        Published listing fields are retained while the listing is useful, including after a role closes. Raw source
        captures are private and are retained for a configurable period (default 90 days) so that a listing can be
        audited or corrected; after that, raw text and comments are purged while the reviewed listing and its source
        reference remain. Reports are retained while needed to resolve the issue. Anonymous analytics events are
        retained for aggregate reporting and are not tied to individuals. Candidate email records are removed 180
        days after the last redirect to the employer's application page. Pending verification codes expire after 10 minutes.
      </p>

      <h2>Your choices</h2>
      <p>
        You can browse without providing any personal data. If you shared an email before continuing to an application
        and want it removed, contact us through the report form and identify the job and email address. If you sent a
        report with a contact email and want it removed, describe the report. Because analytics are anonymous, we
        cannot look up or delete an individual browsing history — we do not have one.
      </p>

      <h2>Security</h2>
      <p>
        Admin routes are protected server-side, database access is restricted with row-level security, secrets are kept
        in server-side environment variables, and raw source text is not publicly readable. No system is perfectly
        secure; if you believe you have found a vulnerability, please report it privately through the community site
        rather than publicly disclosing it.
      </p>

      <h2>Changes</h2>
      <p>
        We may update this policy as the directory changes. The date at the top of the page shows the current version.
        Material changes will be reflected here before they take effect.
      </p>

      <h2>Contact</h2>
      <p>
        Privacy questions can be sent through the <a href="/report">report form</a> or the
        <a href="https://www.linkedin.com/company/hustlercommunity" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"
          >official Hustler Community LinkedIn page</a
        >.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</PublicLayout>
